# Environment
.env

# Go
/apps/edge-api/tmp/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Rust (apps/desktop's Tauri crate)
**/target/
/apps/desktop/dist/
# tauri-build regenerates these editor/IDE JSON schemas on every build
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# Dependencies
# /vendor/* (not /vendor/, so git still traverses into vendor/ to evaluate
# the negation below — a parent directory that is itself excluded cannot
# have its children re-included).
/vendor/*
# apps/agent-engine (issue #305/#308) intentionally vendors and commits a
# trimmed, patched copy of OpenHands's software-agent-sdk; see
# vendor/openhands/VENDORING.md.
!/vendor/openhands/
node_modules/
package-lock.json
# Apps whose CI job installs with `npm ci` need their lockfile committed, so
# they are re-included from the blanket rule above. apps/web-console and
# apps/desktop predate that rule and are already tracked, which is why they
# need no negation here.
!/apps/agent-console/package-lock.json

# Rust (apps/desktop-sandbox) — Cargo.lock is committed for reproducible
# builds of the codex-bwrap binary; only the build output is ignored.
/apps/desktop-sandbox/target/
/apps/desktop-sandbox/*/target/

# apps/agent-engine runtime image: the Apptainer SIF is a multi-GB build
# artifact (built in CI or via deploy/apptainer/build.sh), never committed.
/deploy/apptainer/*.sif

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker
.docker/

# Generated
SBOM.json
SBOM-go.json
SBOM-npm.json
/packages/openai-contract/generated/
/apps/edge-api/internal/generated/
__pycache__/
/apps/web-console/playwright-report/
# Playwright's output dir. The glob, not the exact name: `--output=<dir>` is
# how you keep two runs' traces apart when measuring flakiness, and a run
# named anything other than test-results/ was landing traces and videos in
# `git status` where an `add -A` could commit them.
/apps/web-console/test-results*/
/apps/web-console/playwright-report-chat-coverage/
/apps/web-console/chat-coverage-report/
/apps/web-console/e2e/chat-coverage/.auth/
# Interaction coverage gate output. Regenerated on every run and specific to
# the origin it ran against, so it travels as a CI artifact and a Playwright
# attachment rather than as a committed file that would go stale silently.
/apps/web-console/interaction-coverage/
# Added by code-review-graph
.code-review-graph/

# Claude Code (user-local)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Caveman compression backups
*.original.md

# local caches and scratch
graphify-out/
.tmp-gallery/
.tmp-shots/
.playwright-mcp/
gh-cli-cache/
node-compile-cache/
supabase/.temp/
/q-*.png
/v-*.png
/r1-*.png
/rev-*.png

# Playwright/browser storage-state fixtures. writeStorageState() in
# tests/e2e/support/live-auth.mjs (and the older phase-19 auth.setup.ts) dumps
# a live GoTrue session (access_token + refresh_token JWTs) into one of
# these at runtime. The two known .auth/ directories already carry their own
# local .gitignore, but that protection is per-directory, not repo-wide: a
# 2026-08-09 scratch run wrote the same shape of file (shot-state.json)
# outside any .auth/ dir, and it stayed off git only because it was outside
# the repo tree, not because anything here would have stopped it. Ignored
# globally so no future storage-state dump, wherever it lands inside the
# repo, is ever stageable.
**/.auth/
**/*storageState*.json
**/*storage-state*.json
**/*-state.json

# OpenWolf per-tool-call telemetry. The hooks in .wolf/hooks/ rewrite these on
# every Read, Write, and Edit, so tracking them makes every session dirty the
# working tree continuously: `git pull --ff-only` gets blocked by churn that
# regenerates between commands, and parallel agents in separate worktrees each
# produce a different, equally valid version of the same file. All of it is
# derived from the working tree or from one session's activity, so none of it
# belongs in git.
#
# Durable OpenWolf knowledge stays tracked and reviewable: cerebrum.md,
# decisions.md, buglog.jsonl, GOAL.md, fleet.json, cost-ledger.md, and the hook
# sources themselves.
.wolf/anatomy.md
.wolf/memory.md
.wolf/token-ledger.json
.wolf/hooks/_session.json
# Generated projection of the tracked .wolf/buglog.jsonl, rebuilt by the
# session-start hook (or `node .wolf/hooks/bugstore.js sync`) so that
# `openwolf bug search` and the dashboard keep working. It also carries the
# post-write hook's `auto-detected` guesses for the rest of the session, which is
# why it is generated rather than tracked.
.wolf/buglog.json
